{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789209152,"nonce":"OOzcNrWB+EReHtNI150tDRMTabQ=","title":"RefOffset scales by bytes in the LLVM tier and the interpreter, by element size in Cranelift and HashLink","message":"HashLink's ORefOffset advances in elements of the destination HREF's tparam (hl_type_size(dst-\u003et-\u003etparam), jit.c). Cranelift does that (codegen.rs, bails on a non-HREF dst). The LLVM arm (opcode.rs RefOffset, moving to memory.rs) GEPs i8 by the raw index, and both interpreter walkers (interpreter/mod.rs, ssa.rs) add the raw index to the pointer. Three engines disagree; the corpus has no RefOffset (0 on test_stdlib), so a fixture is needed first (hl.Ref offset arithmetic over Int and Float), judged against stock HashLink.","files":null}]}